<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Noguera Ribagorzana</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Noguera Ribagorzana is a river of the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a> that rises near the Aragon–Catalonia border and flows south into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/segre">Segre</a>. For much of its course it marks the boundary between Aragon and Catalonia, and its valley belonged to the medieval county of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ribagorza">Ribagorza</a>. It is heavily dammed for hydroelectric power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/noguera-ribagorzana.jpg" alt="Noguera Ribagorzana" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ainhoa from Catalunya · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Embassament_de_Canelles.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
